                "en": "In the workbook, how full the aircraft is and how much it burns are two *independent* settings: adding passengers per flight does not raise fuel use per aircraft-kilometre. That is right if the extra passengers fill empty seats, and wrong if bigger aircraft are needed. Short-haul is where this shows best: between 2000 and 2019 it gained 39.3% passengers per flight — mostly through bigger aircraft — and its fuel use per aircraft-kilometre rose by only 2.6%, from 67.3 to 69.1 kWh. The size effect is real, then, but over the same period technical progress almost entirely cancelled it."
