            "en": "Keeping half the past trend is cautious, and open to question on three counts. First the period: the trend is measured to 2023, a year when traffic had not returned to normal and fuel use per kilometre is abnormally high; stopped in 2019, the same rule would give a more demanding objective on long-haul and an almost neutral one on short-haul. Then the rule itself: mechanically applying \"half the trend\" amounts, on intra-European, to extending a deterioration by half, with no argument of its own. Finally, the real blind spot is elsewhere: the non-CO₂ effects of flying at altitude, contrails included, are not in this model at all."
